+
+## Decisions & Alternatives
+
+| Decision | Alternatives Considered | Rationale |
+|---|---|---|
+| Lookup backend: local embedded SQLite index, built and validated on each kiosk from the active snapshot | On-site HTTPS directory — one centrally maintained index and smaller kiosk updates, but lookups depend on the lab network and need service-timeout handling. Managed search service — less index maintenance and room for richer search later, but recurring cost, credentials, and external connectivity. | Both alternatives require network connectivity at lookup time, which conflicts with the HLD tenet that lookup completes using files on the kiosk with no runtime network access (`docs/high-level-design.md` § Tenets) — kiosks have no network route during normal operation. The embedded index is the only candidate that keeps validation, build, and lookup entirely inside this node. The certificate interface is identical under every candidate. |
